@startuml ocaml_usage_timing
title When the functional programming layer is used

skinparam backgroundColor #F7F3EA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Aptos"
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam ArrowColor #53635B
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

start
:Build container or local environment;
:Compile dagentsc with dune;
note right
  This happens before the app runs.
  Dockerfiles copy the compiled CLI into services.
end note

:Start service or demo app;
:Set DAGENTSC_BIN and service URLs;

if (Incoming app/API request?) then (yes)
  :Call Dagents service API\nor app-specific endpoint;
  :Service builds a typed JSON request;
  :Invoke dagentsc as a process;
  :OCaml validates / plans / routes / renders;
  :Service executes runtime work\nor returns the plan to the caller;
else (deployment operation)
  :Core service receives workload spec;
  :Manifest compiler renders Kubernetes bundle;
endif

if (ML training or database I/O?) then (yes)
  :Handled by Python/Spring/runtime adapters;
  note right
    OCaml does not train models,
    keep sockets open, or read production data.
  end note
else (planner work)
  :Handled by OCaml modules;
endif

stop
@enduml
